  "package_id": "berge-path-saturation",
  "formal_scope": "Lean 4.35.0 proves, for actual three-uniform hypergraphs, Berge paths and saturation under every absent triple, that t disjoint loose d-cycles with two isolated vertices are Berge-P_{d+2}-saturated for every d ≥ 3, that the explicit 34-vertex hypergraph is Berge-P₁₀-saturated with 16 hyperedges, and that the three-uniform case of the conjecture fails for every m ≥ 10. The matching lower bound, the exact formula and the uniqueness of extremal hypergraphs have conventional proofs that use two results of the source paper.",
